[{:db/id "32a582f3-ec49-5904-99aa-53c73288aae3" :answer/id #uuid "32a582f3-ec49-5904-99aa-53c73288aae3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-15,102⟩\\cdot ⟨x - 3,\\,y - 3⟩=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "4b48aec1-60e5-583c-ada6-a775d24ebc37" :answer/id #uuid "4b48aec1-60e5-583c-ada6-a775d24ebc37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨15,102⟩\\cdot ⟨x - 3,\\,y + 3⟩=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "90b092f8-0fdd-5bdc-a2ce-b5869f85c49f" :answer/id #uuid "90b092f8-0fdd-5bdc-a2ce-b5869f85c49f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨102,15⟩\\cdot ⟨x - 3,\\,y - 3⟩=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "6fd2df2a-bf80-53d8-92cf-7e86fd6efaab" :answer/id #uuid "6fd2df2a-bf80-53d8-92cf-7e86fd6efaab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨15,102⟩\\cdot ⟨x + 3,\\,y - 3⟩=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "00042721-b3b3-5fbd-b6e7-5fc25785342e" :answer/id #uuid "00042721-b3b3-5fbd-b6e7-5fc25785342e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨15,102⟩\\cdot ⟨x - 3,\\,y - 3⟩=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "e75251e7-9449-527e-a205-be7072ce45be" :answer-field/id #uuid "e75251e7-9449-527e-a205-be7072ce45be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["32a582f3-ec49-5904-99aa-53c73288aae3" "4b48aec1-60e5-583c-ada6-a775d24ebc37" "90b092f8-0fdd-5bdc-a2ce-b5869f85c49f" "6fd2df2a-bf80-53d8-92cf-7e86fd6efaab" "00042721-b3b3-5fbd-b6e7-5fc25785342e"] :answer-field/correct "00042721-b3b3-5fbd-b6e7-5fc25785342e" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "ed4b53f0-5376-5776-9478-e43f57923282" :question/id #uuid "ed4b53f0-5376-5776-9478-e43f57923282" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y)=- 5 x^{2} + 5 x y^{2} + 2 y^{2}$, find the equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(3,3).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent line to the level curve $f(x,y)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(3,3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(- 5 x^{2} + 5 x y^{2} + 2 y^{2})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(- 5 x^{2} + 5 x y^{2} + 2 y^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =(- 10 x + 5 y^{2})\\,i+(10 x y + 4 y)\\,j \\\\ ∇f(3,3) & =(- 10 (3) + 5 (3)^{2})\\,i+(10 (3) (3) + 4 (3))\\,j \\\\  & =(15)\\,i+(102)\\,j \\\\  & =⟨15,102⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(3,3)\\cdot ⟨x-(3),\\,y-(3)⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨15,102⟩\\cdot ⟨x - 3,\\,y - 3⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["e75251e7-9449-527e-a205-be7072ce45be"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "710f2844-45c8-59bf-880d-fe3c26cb0832" :answer/id #uuid "710f2844-45c8-59bf-880d-fe3c26cb0832" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-49,66⟩\\cdot ⟨x + 1,\\,y + 3⟩=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "e2b2b0d4-a0e4-5086-b86d-dbc7f486d746" :answer/id #uuid "e2b2b0d4-a0e4-5086-b86d-dbc7f486d746" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨66,-49⟩\\cdot ⟨x + 1,\\,y - 3⟩=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "d48dac5a-1d5f-5154-aa25-33bdbfcde65c" :answer/id #uuid "d48dac5a-1d5f-5154-aa25-33bdbfcde65c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨49,66⟩\\cdot ⟨x + 1,\\,y - 3⟩=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "14fa1950-a214-593e-94bb-243b690a1707" :answer/id #uuid "14fa1950-a214-593e-94bb-243b690a1707" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-49,66⟩\\cdot ⟨x + 1,\\,y - 3⟩=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "df36e640-415f-58a4-bc06-4d7c4809c34d" :answer/id #uuid "df36e640-415f-58a4-bc06-4d7c4809c34d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-49,66⟩\\cdot ⟨x - 1,\\,y - 3⟩=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "7baa5690-e3d0-5579-a631-3557bc32676a" :answer-field/id #uuid "7baa5690-e3d0-5579-a631-3557bc32676a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["710f2844-45c8-59bf-880d-fe3c26cb0832" "e2b2b0d4-a0e4-5086-b86d-dbc7f486d746" "d48dac5a-1d5f-5154-aa25-33bdbfcde65c" "14fa1950-a214-593e-94bb-243b690a1707" "df36e640-415f-58a4-bc06-4d7c4809c34d"] :answer-field/correct "14fa1950-a214-593e-94bb-243b690a1707" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "881a79d9-03b1-51ac-8b66-c52a6345dfc8" :question/id #uuid "881a79d9-03b1-51ac-8b66-c52a6345dfc8" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y)=2 x^{2} - 5 x y^{2} + 6 y^{2}$, find the equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(-1,3).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent line to the level curve $f(x,y)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(-1,3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2 x^{2} - 5 x y^{2} + 6 y^{2})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2 x^{2} - 5 x y^{2} + 6 y^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =(4 x - 5 y^{2})\\,i+(- 10 x y + 12 y)\\,j \\\\ ∇f(-1,3) & =(4 (-1) - 5 (3)^{2})\\,i+(- 10 (-1) (3) + 12 (3))\\,j \\\\  & =(-49)\\,i+(66)\\,j \\\\  & =⟨-49,66⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(-1,3)\\cdot ⟨x-(-1),\\,y-(3)⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-49,66⟩\\cdot ⟨x + 1,\\,y - 3⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["7baa5690-e3d0-5579-a631-3557bc32676a"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "25baa447-0f3c-51cd-aaf7-6b3ac00a96e5" :answer/id #uuid "25baa447-0f3c-51cd-aaf7-6b3ac00a96e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨72,-16⟩\\cdot ⟨x + 2,\\,y - 3⟩=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "afc3ae48-4ccd-52e2-bf8b-9d12065c313f" :answer/id #uuid "afc3ae48-4ccd-52e2-bf8b-9d12065c313f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-16,72⟩\\cdot ⟨x - 2,\\,y - 3⟩=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "711d8eaf-84ac-5817-bb06-8bb383e766df" :answer/id #uuid "711d8eaf-84ac-5817-bb06-8bb383e766df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-16,72⟩\\cdot ⟨x + 2,\\,y + 3⟩=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "9def3085-312c-56c4-b6c4-579f38156da9" :answer/id #uuid "9def3085-312c-56c4-b6c4-579f38156da9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨16,72⟩\\cdot ⟨x + 2,\\,y - 3⟩=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "c043f7b5-28da-593e-87dc-f36af21369cc" :answer/id #uuid "c043f7b5-28da-593e-87dc-f36af21369cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-16,72⟩\\cdot ⟨x + 2,\\,y - 3⟩=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "e01f9818-57a3-5956-a213-c06417520ad9" :answer-field/id #uuid "e01f9818-57a3-5956-a213-c06417520ad9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["25baa447-0f3c-51cd-aaf7-6b3ac00a96e5" "afc3ae48-4ccd-52e2-bf8b-9d12065c313f" "711d8eaf-84ac-5817-bb06-8bb383e766df" "9def3085-312c-56c4-b6c4-579f38156da9" "c043f7b5-28da-593e-87dc-f36af21369cc"] :answer-field/correct "c043f7b5-28da-593e-87dc-f36af21369cc" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "d5f68602-add6-5304-86ea-92cd8a4ba23c" :question/id #uuid "d5f68602-add6-5304-86ea-92cd8a4ba23c" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y)=- 5 x^{2} - 4 x y^{2} + 4 y^{2}$, find the equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(-2,3).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent line to the level curve $f(x,y)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(-2,3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(- 5 x^{2} - 4 x y^{2} + 4 y^{2})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(- 5 x^{2} - 4 x y^{2} + 4 y^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =(- 10 x - 4 y^{2})\\,i+(- 8 x y + 8 y)\\,j \\\\ ∇f(-2,3) & =(- 10 (-2) - 4 (3)^{2})\\,i+(- 8 (-2) (3) + 8 (3))\\,j \\\\  & =(-16)\\,i+(72)\\,j \\\\  & =⟨-16,72⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(-2,3)\\cdot ⟨x-(-2),\\,y-(3)⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-16,72⟩\\cdot ⟨x + 2,\\,y - 3⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["e01f9818-57a3-5956-a213-c06417520ad9"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "803e91f0-bba5-5405-ae5a-c091ede06aa4" :answer/id #uuid "803e91f0-bba5-5405-ae5a-c091ede06aa4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-12,-8⟩\\cdot ⟨x + 1,\\,y + 2⟩=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "5c37ef54-3dae-58eb-86ba-e0608831b30c" :answer/id #uuid "5c37ef54-3dae-58eb-86ba-e0608831b30c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-8,-12⟩\\cdot ⟨x + 1,\\,y + 2⟩=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "61b75093-2b8c-58b7-8188-b0952cfe42de" :answer/id #uuid "61b75093-2b8c-58b7-8188-b0952cfe42de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨8,-12⟩\\cdot ⟨x + 1,\\,y + 2⟩=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "caf0597d-ab9c-5a42-82c1-3fe84a63a936" :answer/id #uuid "caf0597d-ab9c-5a42-82c1-3fe84a63a936" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-8,-12⟩\\cdot ⟨x - 1,\\,y + 2⟩=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "7a0b9fd6-d82a-5b2a-959f-b39a6313e958" :answer/id #uuid "7a0b9fd6-d82a-5b2a-959f-b39a6313e958" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-8,-12⟩\\cdot ⟨x + 1,\\,y - 2⟩=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "f8d79453-6692-51e6-8683-1c5f858701cd" :answer-field/id #uuid "f8d79453-6692-51e6-8683-1c5f858701cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["803e91f0-bba5-5405-ae5a-c091ede06aa4" "5c37ef54-3dae-58eb-86ba-e0608831b30c" "61b75093-2b8c-58b7-8188-b0952cfe42de" "caf0597d-ab9c-5a42-82c1-3fe84a63a936" "7a0b9fd6-d82a-5b2a-959f-b39a6313e958"] :answer-field/correct "5c37ef54-3dae-58eb-86ba-e0608831b30c" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "1c9b715c-7ccb-51aa-804e-8cbcc40004a8" :question/id #uuid "1c9b715c-7ccb-51aa-804e-8cbcc40004a8" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y)=6 x^{2} + x y^{2} + 4 y^{2}$, find the equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(-1,-2).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent line to the level curve $f(x,y)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(-1,-2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(6 x^{2} + x y^{2} + 4 y^{2})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(6 x^{2} + x y^{2} + 4 y^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =(12 x + y^{2})\\,i+(2 x y + 8 y)\\,j \\\\ ∇f(-1,-2) & =(12 (-1) + (-2)^{2})\\,i+(2 (-1) (-2) + 8 (-2))\\,j \\\\  & =(-8)\\,i+(-12)\\,j \\\\  & =⟨-8,-12⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(-1,-2)\\cdot ⟨x-(-1),\\,y-(-2)⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-8,-12⟩\\cdot ⟨x + 1,\\,y + 2⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["f8d79453-6692-51e6-8683-1c5f858701cd"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "546d86d2-b987-5441-a035-ea8120764307" :answer/id #uuid "546d86d2-b987-5441-a035-ea8120764307" :answer/typ